  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3f17f626-07ec-56e3-b232-a93e9becfb6a" activityNameId="e3a0ea53-759d-5fb2-b059-966c3ca38601" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, lead smelter slag, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, lead smelter slag, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% lead smelter slag; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 595070; H n.a.; C n.a.; S 27000; N n.a.; P 1580; B n.a.; Cl n.a.; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag 52; As 998.71; Ba 1810; Cd 14; Co 123; Cr 150; Cu 1303.8; Hg n.a.; Mn 54300; Mo 57; Ni 87; Pb 12497; Sb 123; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V 69; Zn 21755; Be n.a.; Sc 7; Sr 1283; Ti 1690; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 280030; Fe n.a.; Ca n.a.; Al n.a.; K n.a.; Mg n.a.; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%. ;; UUID: 8adee341-8fc9-4369-9d86-94afdf916d9d
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Minimal long-term emissions are the emissions until the carbonate buffer in the landfill is used up. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr).
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8adee341-8fc9-4369-9d86-94afdf916d9d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
